 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Repaired the order date on the existing project '{{v1}}' to 2026-11-15 (project ID {{v3}}, per the details URL /en/admin/project/{{v3}}/details); no new project was created and no other field was changed. The order-date input on /en/admin/project/{{v3}}/edit is a Litepicker-driven field (data-datepicker=\"on\", data-format=\"M/D/YYYY\", with a pattern that rejects a leading-zero month), which is why typing alone never persisted: I clicked the field, used the picker's next-month control so its header moved from \"October2026\" to \"November2026\", clicked the day-15 cell, which set the field to {{v4}}, then submitted with the form's real Save control (form[name=\"project_edit_form\"] input[type=submit][value=\"Save\"]). Verified three ways: the project details page now displays a row \"Order date {{v4}}\" (it previously showed 10/6/2026), the reopened edit form reads {{v4}}, and the raw server response for the edit page contains value=\"{{v4}}\" for id project_edit_form_orderDate. Name (heading \"{{v1}}\"), description (\"Bench run {{v2}} project for automation verification.\"), customer (\"Bench Customer\") and order number (\"PO-4471\", project number 0005) are unchanged.",
